# Gurbalib project context

This project is based on **Gurbalib**, a lightweight LPC mudlib for the **DGD** (Dworkin's Game Driver). Code is written in **LPC** (`.c` files), not C despite the extension.

## Stack

- **Driver**: DGD — compile from https://github.com/dworkin/dgd
- **Mudlib**: Gurbalib — https://github.com/sirdude/gurbalib
- **Docs**: `doc/`, `lib/doc/` (use in-game `man` for afun/safun/kfun/kernel/modules)

## Directory layout (`lib/`)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `lib/std/` | Base game classes: room, monster, weapon, armor, container, body, modules |
| `lib/sys/` | System layer: daemons, safuns, command framework, telnet, FTP, Intermud |
| `lib/kernel/` | Driver interface: afuns, driver config (`local_config.h`) |
| `lib/domains/` | Game content — rooms, monsters, objects, areas (primary place for new content) |
| `lib/cmds/` | Player-facing commands |
| `lib/sys/cmds/` | Wizard and admin commands |
| `lib/daemons/` | Long-lived service objects |
| `lib/data/` | Runtime data (messages, player saves, etc.) |
| `lib/logs/` | Driver and mud logs — check `lib/logs/gurba-driver.log` on startup failures |

## Inheritance hierarchy

- Game objects inherit from `/std/*` base classes (e.g. `inherit "/std/room"`)
- Commands inherit `M_COMMAND` (defined in `/sys/lib/modules/m_command.c`)
- Modules use `inherit "/std/modules/m_*"` or `inherit "/sys/lib/modules/m_*"` for composable behavior
- Use **absolute paths** in inherit statements: `inherit "/std/monster"` not relative paths

## Function resolution order

When a function exists at multiple layers: **safun > afun > kfun**. Prefer existing safuns/afuns over reimplementing.

## Configuration

- `mud.dgd` — driver config (copy from `mud.dgd.examp`)
- `lib/kernel/include/local_config.h` — mud-specific defines (copy from `local_config.h.default`)
- `lib/std/include/local_config.h` — optional std-layer overrides (e.g. `DISABLE_FTP`)

## Key conventions

- Objects are **cloned**, not instantiated — use `clone_object()` and call `setup()` on the clone
- Paths use forward slashes from lib root: `/domains/myarea/rooms/town_square.c`
- After adding or changing commands, admins must run **`rehash`**
- After editing LPC files in a running mud, use wizard **`update <file>`** to reload
- Do not edit `lib/kernel/` or `lib/sys/` casually — prefer extending via `lib/domains/` and `lib/std/modules/`

## Reference examples

- Minimal room: `lib/domains/required/rooms/start.c`
- Minimal monster: `lib/domains/required/monsters/rat.c`
- Wizard command: `lib/sys/cmds/wiz/clone.c`
- Style guide: `lib/doc/help/wiz/style`
